  } else if (containsPanFry && !containsSaute) {
    s"$text describes pan-frying. The similarities between sautéing and pan-frying are that both techniques involve cooking food in a hot pan with oil. The differences are that pan-frying typically involves cooking larger pieces of food over medium heat for a longer period of time, while sautéing involves quickly cooking small pieces of food over high heat."
