Here is a JavaScript code that generates a monochromatic color scheme using shades from a Pantone color palette:
```
const pantoneColor = '#F5DF4D'; // replace with desired Pantone color
const shades = 5; // number of shades to generate
const colorScheme = [];
for (let i = 0; i < shades; i++) {
  const shade = i / (shades - 1);
  const newColor = tinycolor(pantoneColor).lighten(shade * 100).toHexString();
  colorScheme.push(newColor);
}
console.log(colorScheme);
```
This code uses the `tinycolor` library to generate shades of the desired Pantone color. The `lighten()` method is used to adjust the lightness of the color, with the amount of lightness determined by the shade number. The resulting color scheme is an array of hex color codes.
