Here's a C++ program that takes user input of a name and age, then calculates and prints the estimated date of their 100th birthday:
```
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <chrono>
using namespace std;
int main() {
  // Get user input
  string name;
  int age;
  cout << "Enter your name: ";
  getline(cin, name);
  cout << "Enter your age: ";
  cin >> age;
  // Calculate estimated date of 100th birthday
  auto now = chrono::system_clock::now();
  auto now_time = chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(now);
  auto tm = *localtime(&now_time);
  int current_year = tm.tm_year + 1900;
  int years_to_100 = 100 - age;
  int estimated_year_of_100th_birthday = current_year + years_to_100;
  tm.tm_year = estimated_year_of_100th_birthday - 1900;
  auto estimated_date_of_100th_birthday = chrono::system_clock::from_time_t(mktime(&tm));
  // Print result
  cout << name << ", you will turn 100 on ";
  cout << chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(estimated_date_of_100th_birthday);
  cout << "." << endl;
  return 0;
}
```
This program uses the `<chrono>` library to get the current date and time, calculate the estimated year of the user's 100th birthday, and print the result in a human-readable format. Note that this program assumes that the user's birthday has already passed this year. If the user's birthday is later in the year, the estimated date of their 100th birthday may be slightly off.

JavaScript can be leveraged in various ways to automate social media promotion for small businesses. Here are three distinct and intricate examples with corresponding strategies:
1. Sentiment Analysis for Optimizing Post Content:
One way to optimize social media promotion is by analyzing the sentiment of the post content. Sentiment analysis is a technique that involves using natural language processing (NLP) to determine the emotional tone of a piece of text. By analyzing the sentiment of the post content, we can ensure that the content is engaging and resonates with the target audience. Here is a breakdown of the technical implementation:
- Use an NLP library like Natural or NLTK to perform sentiment analysis on the post content.
- Analyze the sentiment score and categorize it as positive, negative, or neutral.
- Based on the sentiment score, customize the post content to make it more engaging and appealing to the target audience.
- Use a social media automation tool like Hootsuite or Buffer to schedule the post at the optimal time for maximum engagement.
Benefits: 
- By analyzing the sentiment of the post content, we can ensure that the content is relevant and resonates with the target audience.
- Customizing the post content based on sentiment can increase engagement and drive more traffic to the business website.
Drawbacks: 
- Sentiment analysis may not always be accurate, especially for complex or nuanced topics.
- Customizing the post content based on sentiment may require additional effort and resources.
Code Snippet:
```
const natural = require('natural');
const analyzer = new natural.SentimentAnalyzer();
const stemmer = natural.PorterStemmer;
const content = "I just tried this new product and it's amazing!";
const sentimentScore = analyzer.getSentiment(stemmer.tokenizeAndStem(content));
console.log(sentimentScore); // Output: 0.8 (Positive sentiment)
```
2. Machine Learning Algorithms for Predicting Optimal Posting Times:
Another way to automate social media promotion is by using machine learning algorithms to predict the optimal posting times. By analyzing historical data and user behavior, we can train a machine learning model to predict the best times to post for maximum engagement. Here is a breakdown of the technical implementation:
- Collect historical data on user engagement for each social media platform.
- Use a machine learning library like TensorFlow or Scikit-learn to train a model to predict the optimal posting times.
- Use the trained model to generate a schedule for posting on each social media platform.
- Use a social media automation tool like Hootsuite or Buffer to schedule the posts at the predicted optimal times.
Benefits: 
- By using machine learning algorithms to predict the optimal posting times, we can maximize engagement and reach a larger audience.
- Automating the scheduling process can save time and resources for small businesses.
Drawbacks: 
- Machine learning algorithms require a large amount of data to train accurately.
- Predictions may not always be accurate and may require manual adjustments.
Code Snippet:
```
const tf = require('@tensorflow/tfjs-node');
const data = [
  { dayOfWeek: 'Monday', hourOfDay: 9, engagement: 0.5 },
  { dayOfWeek: 'Monday', hourOfDay: 12, engagement: 0.8 },
  { dayOfWeek: 'Monday', hourOfDay: 15, engagement: 0.6 },
  { dayOfWeek: 'Tuesday', hourOfDay: 9, engagement: 0.7 },
  { dayOfWeek: 'Tuesday', hourOfDay: 12, engagement: 0.9 },
  { dayOfWeek: 'Tuesday', hourOfDay: 15, engagement: 0.5 },
  // ...
];
const model = tf.sequential();
model.add(tf.layers.dense({ inputShape: [2], units: 1 }));
model.compile({ optimizer: 'sgd', loss: 'meanSquaredError' });
const xs = tf.tensor2d(data.map(({ dayOfWeek, hourOfDay }) => [dayOfWeek, hourOfDay]));
const ys = tf.tensor2d(data.map(({ engagement }) => [engagement]));
model.fit(xs, ys, { epochs: 10 }).then(() => {
  const monday9am = tf.tensor2d([['Monday', 9]]);
  const monday12pm = tf.tensor2d([['Monday', 12]]);
  const monday3pm = tf.tensor2d([['Monday', 15]]);
  const tuesday9am = tf.tensor2d([['Tuesday', 9]]);
  const tuesday12pm = tf.tensor2d([['Tuesday', 12]]);
  const tuesday3pm = tf.tensor2d([['Tuesday', 15]]);
  // ...
  console.log(`Monday 9am engagement: ${model.predict(monday9am)}`);
  console.log(`Tuesday 12pm engagement: ${model.predict(tuesday12pm)}`);
});
```
3. Dynamic Chatbots for Adapting to User Conversations:
A third way to automate social media promotion is by creating dynamic chatbots that can adapt to a user's conversation. Chatbots can be used to answer frequently asked questions, provide product recommendations, and engage with customers. By using natural language processing and machine learning algorithms, we can create chatbots that can understand and respond to user queries. Here is a breakdown of the technical implementation:
- Use a chatbot framework like Botpress or Dialogflow to create a chatbot.
- Train the chatbot using machine learning algorithms to understand and respond to user queries.
- Use sentiment analysis to determine the emotional tone of the user's message and customize the response accordingly.
- Use the chatbot to engage with customers and promote the business on social media platforms.
Benefits: 
- Chatbots can provide 24/7 customer support and improve customer satisfaction.
- By engaging with customers on social media platforms, chatbots can increase brand awareness and drive traffic to the business website.
Drawbacks: 
- Chatbots may not always understand complex or nuanced queries.
- Customizing responses based on sentiment may require additional effort and resources.
Code Snippet:
```
const botpress = require('botpress');
const bot = botpress.init();
bot.hear(/hello/i, (event) => {
  const sentiment = analyzeSentiment(event.text);
  const response = sentiment === 'positive' ? 'Hi there, how can I help you today?' : 'Hello, is there anything I can assist you with?';
  event.reply(response);
});
