How can I use C++ code to extract and display details about the memory usage of a specific process? Can you provide me with three different codes that would allow me to monitor the memory usage of a process and display the results in different formats, such as total memory used, memory used by a specific component, and percentage of memory usage? Please provide examples for each code.
Here's an example C++ code to display total memory used by a specific process:
#include <windows.h>
#include <psapi.h>
#include <stdio.h>
void PrintMemoryInfo(DWORD processID)
{
    HANDLE hProcess;
    PROCESS_MEMORY_COUNTERS pmc;
    // Get a handle to the process.
    hProcess = OpenProcess(PROCESS_QUERY_INFORMATION | PROCESS_VM_READ, FALSE, processID);
    if (NULL == hProcess)
