How can I incorporate the Fibonacci sequence into my PHP program to generate a unique color palette for an image, based on the number of pixels in the image? Can you provide a sample code snippet to demonstrate this?
Here's a PHP code snippet that generates a unique color palette based on the Fibonacci sequence:
<?php
function generate_color_palette($num_pixels) {
  $fib_sequence = array(0, 1);
  while(count($fib_sequence) < $num_pixels) {
    $next_num = $fib_sequence[count($fib_sequence) - 1] + $fib_sequence[count($fib_sequence) - 2];
    array_push($fib_sequence, $next_num);
  }

  $color_palette = array();
  foreach($fib_sequence as $num) {
    $color = dechex($num % 16777215);
    array_push($color_palette, $color);
  }

  return $color_palette;
}
$num_pixels = 1000;
$color_palette = generate_color_palette($num_pixels);
echo "Color palette for $num_pixels pixels:<br>";
foreach($color_palette as $color) {
  echo "<div style='background-color: #$color; width: 50px; height: 50px; display: inline-block;'></div>";
}
?>
This code generates a Fibonacci sequence with a length equal to the number of pixels in the image, and then converts each number in the sequence to a hexadecimal color code. The resulting color palette is then displayed as a series of square divs with the corresponding background color.

